<title>USA: Textron's Cessna gets $600 mln jet order.</title>
<headline>Textron's Cessna gets $600 mln jet order.</headline>
<dateline>WICHITA, Kan. 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cessna Aircraft Co and Executive Jet Aviation (EJA) said on Tuesday they reached a $600 million agreement for EJA to buy 25 Citation Xs and 20 Citation VIIs for its fleet of fractional ownership aircraft.</p>
<p>Deliveries are slated to begin next year, a statement from the companies said.</p>
<p>Cessna is a unit of Textron Inc.</p>
<p>Cessna said the purchase agreement, which will extend into the 21st Century, is the largest order it has ever booked and , to its knowledge, the largest business jet purchase in history.</p>
</text>
